Licence not yet chosen.

PRODUCT_SPEC section 24 lists the licence as an open decision that must be resolved before public
release. Until an ADR records that decision, no licence is granted and all rights are reserved by the
copyright holders.

This blocks distribution, not development.

Two constraints will shape the choice, and both are recorded here so the decision is made with them
in view:

  1. PRODUCT_SPEC 3.4 and 22.13 forbid copying code from the official Audiobookshelf application
     unless this project deliberately adopts a compatible licence and records the provenance. No code
     has been copied from it. If that ever changes, the licence decision must come first, not after.

  2. The working title is deliberately unofficial. Whatever licence is chosen, the final branding must
     not imply endorsement by the Audiobookshelf project, and the Audiobookshelf logo and official
     branding must not be used without explicit permission (PRODUCT_SPEC 1).

Third-party dependencies keep their own licences. A Software Bill of Materials is required before
release (PRODUCT_SPEC 18).
